internet was built for humans clicking buttons; the next internet is being built for agents acting on their behalf — discovering services, negotiating terms, executing settlement, and learning from physical demonstration. Two infrastructure layers are forming in parallel: a payment stack for autonomous agents at machine speed, and a data stack for agents to learn from human physical experience. Neither works alone; together they describe the architectural floor of Physical AI. Agentic commerce is already measurable — OpenAI's Instant Checkout, Polymarket's $9B volume, Audius's real-time artist payouts, and over 40% of docs traffic now from AI agents. Three protocols standardize agentic commerce: UCP (discovery), AP2 (verifiable credentials), and x402 (HTTP 402 payments). The stablecoin track dominates machine economy — sub-second finality, 24/7 operation, atomic FX, conditionality plus escrow. Agents cannot be their own last line of defense — five-dimension policy engines govern spending limits, counterparty allowlists, transaction restrictions, time controls, and escalation thresholds. Egocentric data at production scale requires authentic activity, stable framing, diverse environments, consent governance — 30,000 hours of raw capture yields ~24,000 hours approved. Legacy procurement cannot pay thousands of micro-transactions; stablecoin settlement makes contributor payouts economically viable. DigiRobotics composes both stacks into a single loop where contributors earn instantly and agents procure programmatically.29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-w-0\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"blockquote\\\",\\\"blockquote-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-10 border-l-2 border-[var(--primary)] bg-[var(--primary)]/[0.06] px-6 py-2 font-heading text-xl leading-8 text-white sm:px-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"\\\\n\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"strong\\\",\\\"strong-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"TL;DR:\\\"}]}],\\\"\\\\n\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$2c\\\"}],\\\"\\\\n\\\"]}],\\\"\\\\n\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h2-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Agents That Pay, Humans That Teach\\\"}],\\\"\\\\n\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The internet was built for humans clicking buttons. The next internet is being built for agents acting on their behalf — discovering services, negotiating terms, executing settlement, and learning from physical demonstration. Two infrastructure layers are forming in parallel, largely independent of each other, and both are non-optional for the next decade of machine intelligence: a payment stack that lets autonomous agents transact at machine speed, and a data stack that lets those same agents learn from human physical experience. Neither works alone. Together, they describe the architectural floor of embodied AI.\\\"}],\\\"\\\\n\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h2-1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The Agentic Finance Stack: A New Class of Economic Actor\\\"}],\\\"\\\\n\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Agentic commerce is no longer a forecast — it is a measurable category. AI systems now act as independent economic actors, discovering services, negotiating complex terms, and executing financial settlement with minimal human intervention. The shape of this economy mirrors the transformation algorithmic trading brought to financial markets a decade ago, except it extends autonomous decision-making to all economic activity, not just order matching.\\\"}],\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L2d\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L2e\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L2f\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L30\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L31\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L32\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L33\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L34\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L35\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L36\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L37\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L38\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L39\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L3a\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L3b\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L3c\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L3d\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L3e\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L3f\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L40\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L41\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L42\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L43\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L44\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L45\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L46\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L47\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"$L48\\\"],\\\"$L49\\\"]}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"footer\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"border-t border-white/[.08] bg-[#111620] py-12\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1440px] px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 xl:px-16\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-start\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lb\\\",null,{\\\"src\\\":\\\"/digirobotics/brand/digirobotics-logo.png\\\",\\\"alt\\\":\\\"DigiRobotics.xyz\\\",\\\"width\\\":210,\\\"height\\\":48,\\\"className\\\":\\\"h-auto w-[190px]\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[17px] text-white/60\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Egocentric data for robotics training.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"nav\\\",null,{\\\"aria-label\\\":\\\"Footer navigation\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex max-w-2xl flex-wrap gap-x-7 gap-y-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Contributor\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/#contributors\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Contributor\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Marketplace\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/#marketplace\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Marketplace\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Custom Data\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/#custom-data\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Custom Data\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Capture Gear\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/gear\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Capture Gear\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Articles\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/blog\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Articles\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Agent Demo\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/agent-demo\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Agent Demo\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Privacy \\u0026 Terms\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/#privacy-note\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Privacy \\u0026 Terms\\\"}],\\\"$L4a\\\"]}]]}],\\\"$L4b\\\",\\\"$L4c\\\",\\\"$L4d\\\"]}]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"2d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Three forces are converging to make this real. AI agents as new economic actors — reasoning systems that take action, not just produce text. Stablecoins as the native currency — programmable digital dollars that settle instantly and 24/7. And blockchain rails as open infrastructure — public settlement layers any agent can access without onboarding to a bank.\\\"}]\\n2e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The early consumer entry points are already live. OpenAI's Instant Checkout in ChatGPT is one of the first mass-market implementations of the Agentic Commerce Protocol. Prediction-market platform Polymarket processed over $9 billion in trading volume, with arbitrageurs extracting $40 million in a single year. Audius routes 90% of earnings directly to artists in real time. Over 40% of traffic to docs powered by Mintlify now comes from AI agents, not humans — a leading indicator of where API consumption is heading.\\\"}]\\n2f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The institutional picture is parallel. Treasury management, collateral optimization, liquidity deployment, and counterparty risk assessment are moving from predefined rules to reasoning-based systems that analyze market conditions in real time. The barrier to mass adoption, as one industry framing puts it, \\\\\\\"was never the technology. It was the cognitive load\\\\\\\" — and agents are precisely the layer that absorbs that load on behalf of users.\\\"}]\\n30:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-5\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Three protocols are forming the standardized transaction stack for agentic commerce. UCP (Universal Commerce Protocol) standardizes agent discovery of merchant capabilities through /.well-known/ucp manifests — the equivalent of robots.txt for payments. AP2 (Agent Payments Protocol) introduces Verifiable Digital Credentials (VDCs) that tie agent actions to explicit human mandates, addressing the accountability gap that has slowed enterprise adoption. x402 repurposes HTTP status code 402 (\\\\\\\"Payment Required\\\\\\\") for machine-to-machine payments directly inside API calls — co-developed by Coinbase and Cloudflare, now the de facto payment primitive for agent-driven API consumption.\\\"}]\\n31:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-6\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The numbers behind x402 are the most concrete signal that this is no longer speculative. Within months of its May 2025 launch, x402 processed over 100 million payments across APIs, apps, and AI agents, reaching an annualized run rate of $600 million in volume by the end of 2025. Solana accounts for the majority of x402 payment volume today, but the protocol is rail-agnostic by design.\\\"}]\\n32:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-7\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Legacy infrastructure is meeting this new stack halfway. Visa's Intelligent Commerce platform expanded USDC settlement to Cross River Bank and Lead Bank on Solana, with reported stablecoin settlement volume rising from a $3.5B annualized run rate in November 2025 to roughly $4.5B by mid-January 2026. Mastercard's Agent Pay platform completed live AI agent payment activity in Singapore with DBS and UOB. Circle's Payments Network (CPN) has emerged as an orchestration layer for institutions. The two-track reality that practitioners now describe is clear:\\\"}]\\n33:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-8\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"strong\\\",\\\"strong-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Business governance track (tokenized cards)\\\"}],\\\" — will dominate retail and consumer commerce, where liability and dispute frameworks already exist.\\\"]}]\\n34:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-9\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"strong\\\",\\\"strong-0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Native settlement track (stablecoins)\\\"}],\\\" — will dominate the machine economy and high-frequency API markets, where sub-cent fees and sub-second finality are non-negotiable.\\\"]}]\\n35:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-10\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The defining properties of the stablecoin track are deterministic finality (transfers reach irreversible settlement in sub-second time), 24/7 operation (no weekend or holiday windows), atomic FX (orchestration layers execute foreign exchange during the payment itself), and conditionality plus escrow (funds lock and release only when defined conditions are met). These are not features legacy fiat ledgers provide natively — and they are the precise properties autonomous agents require.\\\"}]\\n36:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h2-2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The Security Premise: Agents Cannot Be Their Own Last Line of Defense\\\"}]\\n37:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-11\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"As agents gain spending authority, the threat surface expands. The relevant attack models now include prompt injection, agent impersonation, runaway agent behavior, key compromise, and supply-chain risk. The emerging consensus among infrastructure providers is blunt: an agent should never be the last line of defense against its own failures.\\\"}]\\n38:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-12\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Policy engines are being built around five dimensions. Spending limits set hard caps per transaction, per day, per counterparty. Counterparty allowlists mean agents can only transact with pre-approved entities. Transaction type restrictions limit spending by category or merchant type. Time-based controls establish windows of permitted activity. And escalation thresholds trigger automatic handoff to a human when risk exceeds a defined level.\\\"}]\\n39:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-13\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"This is the governance layer that will determine whether agentic commerce scales safely past the experimental phase.\\\"}]\\n3a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h2-3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The Other Half: Egocentric Data at Production Scale\\\"}]\\n3b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-14\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"If agentic finance is the settlement layer for autonomous machines, egocentric data is the training layer. Embodied AI — robots, humanoids, manipulators — cannot be trained on the text and image corpora that built chatbots. They require first-person, sensor-native recordings of humans performing physical tasks: reaching into cabinets, operating machinery, handling objects in cluttered environments.\\\"}]\\n3c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-15\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The collection problem is harder than it looks. Raw first-person footage is abundant and almost useless for policy training. A production-grade egocentric dataset must satisfy several simultaneous constraints. Authentic activity means natural task execution, not staged movements. Stable first-person framing keeps hands, objects, and workspace continuously visible. Diverse environments span residential, industrial, retail, hospitality, agricultural, construction, and service settings. Geographic and demographic diversity recognizes that task distributions vary dramatically across cultures and economies. And consent and governance built in recognizes that first-person video is biometric data under most privacy regimes.\\\"}]\\n3d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-16\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"A recent case study from Shaip illustrates what production-scale collection looks like in practice. The program produced 30,000 hours of egocentric video, of which over 24,000 hours were annotated and approved for model training — a yield rate that reveals how much raw capture is lost to framing errors, idle footage, and quality regressions. Contributors recorded authentic activities using consumer mobile devices (iPhone 11+, Google Pixel 6+, Samsung Galaxy S21+) securely mounted at forehead level at approximately a 45° downward angle — a geometry chosen to keep hands, objects, and workspace in frame simultaneously. Each participant contributed up to 100 approved hours, across the United States and Latin America, spanning household, industrial, and commercial settings.\\\"}]\\n3e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-17\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The workflow design is as important as the hardware. A one-day review cycle with explicit rejection reasons enabled rapid recapture rather than waiting weeks to discover a capture error. An automated mobile application handled submission and location verification. Quality intervention was continuous rather than post-hoc. The resulting dataset was explicitly designed to be robotics-ready — usable for activity recognition, hand-object interaction modeling, and robotic perception without rework.\\\"}]\\n3f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h2-4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Why the Two Stacks Are Co-Dependent\\\"}]\\n40:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-18\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The agentic finance stack and the egocentric data stack are usually discussed in separate communities — crypto-native builders on one side, robotics researchers on the other. They are, in fact, the same problem viewed from two angles.\\\"}]\\n41:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-19\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Consider the economics of a 30,000-hour egocentric dataset. If each contributor produces up to 100 approved hours at a fair per-hour rate, the contribution economy involves hundreds of individuals across multiple countries, each generating dozens of micro-transactions over the project lifecycle. A traditional procurement flow — invoice, approval, batch payment, 30-day settlement — collapses under the weight of that volume. The marginal cost of paying one contributor for one hour of approved footage approaches zero only if the settlement rail itself costs near zero and settles instantly.\\\"}]\\n42:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-20\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"That is exactly what the agentic finance stack provides. The same x402 protocol that processes API micropayments for AI agents can settle contributor payouts for egocentric data — atomically, programmatically, and without human review of each transaction. The same stablecoin settlement that gives Visa and Mastercard sub-second finality can pay a contributor in Latin America the moment their footage passes quality review, with no correspondent banking delays and no FX friction. The same policy engines that constrain runaway agents can govern automated payout flows, enforcing spending limits and counterparty allowlists on data procurement budgets.\\\"}]\\n43:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-21\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The reverse dependency is just as strong. Agentic commerce needs real-world tasks to settle around. The richest, most under-monetized category of real-world task data is physical human activity — the manipulation, locomotion, and tool use that robotics labs are desperate to acquire. Without a marketplace that connects contributors to consumers programmatically, the long tail of physical-world expertise stays locked inside a handful of well-capitalized labs. Without the data that marketplace would surface, embodied AI policies plateau well below their scaling-law potential.\\\"}]\\n44:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h2-5\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The DigiRobotics Connection\\\"}]\\n45:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-22\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"This is the structural gap DigiRobotics is built to close. DigiRobotics is the world's first stablecoin-native marketplace for agentic commerce in real-world robotics data — explicitly designed at the intersection of the two stacks described above.\\\"}]\\n46:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-23\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The mechanics map directly onto the protocols now standardizing the broader agentic commerce ecosystem. Contributors — whether specialized operators with multi-camera rigs or everyday users with accessible capture devices — record egocentric footage of physical tasks, the same category of data that production-scale collection programs have shown requires 30,000+ hours of raw capture to yield a usable training set. That data is tokenized and listed on the marketplace, where AI agents, robotics labs, and humanoid developers can procure it programmatically. Settlement runs over the x402 protocol — the same HTTP-native payment layer processing hundreds of millions of payments across the agentic economy — with transactions executed instantly in stablecoins such as USDG on Arbitrum, keeping gas costs negligible for sub-cent transactions.\\\"}]\\n47:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-24\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The architectural fit is deliberate. DigiRobotics does not reinvent the payment layer or the data layer; it composes them. The stablecoin settlement track that the broader industry has converged on for high-frequency machine payments is the natural rail for contributor payouts at the volume egocentric data collection requires. The x402 protocol that already powers agentic API consumption is the natural primitive for agent-to-agent data procurement. The verifiable credentials and policy-engine patterns emerging in AP2-aligned systems are the natural governance layer for a marketplace where autonomous agents are the buyers.\\\"}]\\n48:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"p-25\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The strategic logic is straightforward. If egocentric data follows the scaling laws now documented in production research — predictable, log-linear gains from each doubling of human demonstration hours — then the bottleneck is not algorithmic. It is distributional. The labs that can internally fund 30,000-hour collection programs are a small handful of names. The planetary-scale tail of human manipulation expertise — across cultures, environments, and task domains — is only reachable through a marketplace that pays contributors instantly and fairly for micro-contributions, in a currency that settles the moment their data is consumed. DigiRobotics is that marketplace: the agentic finance stack and the egocentric data stack, finally wired together as a single loop.\\\"}]\\n49:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-16 border-t border-white/10 pt-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L26\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/blog\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 px-5 py-3 text-[14px] font-semibold transition hover:border-[var(--primary)] hover:text-[var(--primary)]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$La\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"icon\\\":\\\"$1e:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:icon\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"size\\\":16,\\\"aria-hidden\\\":\\\"true\\\"}],\\\" Return to the archive\\\"]}]}]\\n4a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"Contact Us\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"mailto:hello@digirobotics.xyz\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Contact Us\\\"}]\\n4b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"id\\\":\\\"privacy-note\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-10 grid gap-4 border-t border-white/[.08] pt-6 text-[13px] leading-5 text-white/45 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto]\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Privacy and terms notices will be published before campaign enrollment or data collection begins. Contact the team for Phase 1 information.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"© 2026 DigiRobotics\\\"}]]}]\\n4c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-6 flex items-center gap-4 text-white/45\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-white/45 hover:text-white transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$La\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"icon\\\":\\\"$14:props:children:0:props:children:props:icon\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"size\\\":18,\\\"aria-hidden\\\":\\\"true\\\"}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"#\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-white/45 hover:text-white transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$La\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"icon\\\":\\\"$14:props:children:1:props:children:props:icon\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"size\\\":18,\\\"aria-hidden\\\":\\\"true\\\"}]}]]}]\\n4d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[.12em] text-white/35\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Agent-compatible payment workflows powered by stablecoins and x402. Phase 1 infrastructure.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rsc":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n3:I[60203,[\"66609\",\"static/chunks/66609-81fc326aefa2b35a.js\",\"17112\",\"static/chunks/17112-6d02a7878e38f17b.js\",\"96048\",\"static/chunks/96048-94353edf3fef0226.js\",\"37024\",\"static/chunks/37024-473db45fa25438c6.js\",\"7177\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-9ceac550056e754f.js\"],\"ThirdwebSessionProvider\"]\n4:I[35682,[\"66609\",\"static/chunks/66609-81fc326aefa2b35a.js\",\"17112\",\"static/chunks/17112-6d02a7878e38f17b.js\",\"96048\",\"static/chunks/96048-94353edf3fef0226.js\",\"37024\",\"static/chunks/37024-473db45fa25438c6.js\",\"7177\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-9ceac550056e754f.js\"],\"CartProvider\"]\n5:I[76826,[\"66609\",\"static/chunks/66609-81fc326aefa2b35a.js\",\"17112\",\"static/chunks/17112-6d02a7878e38f17b.js\",\"96048\",\"static/chunks/96048-94353edf3fef0226.js\",\"37024\",\"static/chunks/37024-473db45fa25438c6.js\",\"7177\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-9ceac550056e754f.js\"],\"AuthFlowProvider\"]\n6:I[57121,[],\"\"]\n7:I[78007,[\"99489\",\"static/chunks/99489-7b4b74c1a59849db.js\",\"5772\",\"static/chunks/5772-2ad3d6bb0136fa62.js\",\"57304\",\"static/ch